NAME
    true - exit with a success status

SYNOPSIS
    true

DESCRIPTION
    Does nothing and always exits with status 0. Intended for loops and
    conditional placeholders such as 'while true; do ...; done'.

EXAMPLES
    true
    echo $?

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    false(1), test(1), if(1), while(1)
